WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.680
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:06.270
At some point in your life you may have become
frustrated with modern day life.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:12.210
The awful music, long work hours, you complain
that everyone’s living through social media,

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:14.900
rather than actually living.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:19.980
You may even foolishly believe that life in
the past was superior and that you were born

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.570
at the wrong time.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:25.400
You may think that life was simpler back then,
less hectic and stressful perhaps.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:30.929
But in reality how good or bad was pre-industrial
life?

00:00:30.929 --> 00:00:33.540
Before machinery and modern medicine.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:39.130
If we go back to the middle-ages or even all
the way back to the Roman empire, was life

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:42.330
ever any better than it is now?

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:48.620
Let’s take a dirty detour and flirt with
the filthy past to discover what it was really

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.840
like to live in the time of the history books.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.360
So, why a dirty detour into the past?

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:02.790
Because ladies and gents, the past was disgusting,
utterly, down-right filthy.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.041
Cities were also disease ridden.

00:01:04.041 --> 00:01:06.810
The bigger the city, the filthier it was.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.299
Human’s are pretty disgusting like that.

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:15.139
The biggest contributor to this problem was
obviously the sewers, or lack of.

00:01:15.139 --> 00:01:21.130
Until the last 200 years most cities around
the world relied on a sewerage system no more

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:24.979
advanced than throwing your waste out your
window and hoping it doesn’t land on your

00:01:24.979 --> 00:01:26.749
wife’s head.

00:01:26.749 --> 00:01:33.780
Some fancier cities though, like ancient Rome
and London had open sewers, how opulent.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:38.530
To put it crudely, open sewers were no more
than a river of shit running past your front

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:39.549
door.

00:01:39.549 --> 00:01:44.719
Very few people had clean running water in
the past, only the wealthy, who’s water

00:01:44.719 --> 00:01:49.340
was delivered through lead pipes which gave
them heavy metal poisoning.

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:55.670
Wait a minute, back up, weren’t the Romans
credited with creating vast underground sewerage

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:57.030
systems?

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:02.500
Well yes, but they only built those in the
dwellings of the upper-class.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:11.860
They also built some public toilets that lead
to underground sewers.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:17.930
Despite them having sewers we know from the
history books that the majority of the lower

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:24.660
class in ancient Rome and elsewhere, still
chose to chuck their waste onto the street,

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.570
it’s just easier I guess.

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:32.510
And in smaller towns and villages across the
world, all throughout history, dumping your

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:38.000
waste onto the street, or all over your neighbour’s
cabbages, has been the standard way to dispose

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.270
of it.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:44.870
Interestingly, emptying waste out of your
window was actually illegal in medieval London,

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:48.090
that didn’t stop most people from doing
it though.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:52.560
The recommended method of waste disposal in
London was actually to dump it in the river

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:58.730
Thames, which is where thousands of people
also got their drinking water from, nice.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:03.820
So what happened to the endless waste piling
up on the street?

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:09.060
Well, sewage collectors, known as “muck
rakers” would roam the streets and collect

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:14.160
all the waste then take it to local farmers
to sell as fertiliser.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:19.130
So next time you complain about your job,
just remember, you could be playing Pokemon

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:21.850
Go with human feces for a living.

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:26.620
That’s if you were lucky enough to have
a local shite shoveller.

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:32.480
Some historic accounts tell of streets that
were caked in solidified waste so deep, that

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:36.970
stepping stones had to be built to traverse
them.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:42.320
But that would only have been a minor inconvenience
for your medieval self, you would have been

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:46.710
far too busy trying to stay alive to care
about the filth.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:52.190
Death and disease was everywhere and almost
every disease out there was hideous and meant

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:58.990
certain death, or if you were lucky an amputated
limb, without anesthesia of course.

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:05.280
Diseases such as leprosy, diabetes, dysentery
and measles were rife and there were no cures

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.710
or treatments, like we have today.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:13.630
In fact, before modern medicine if you managed
to reach the age of 40 and your face hadn’t

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:16.660
fallen off yet, then you were incredibly lucky.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:23.680
But it wasn’t all bad, contrary to popular
belief, peasants in the middle ages did eat

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:24.950
rather well.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:28.690
They weren’t starved like books and films
would have us believe.

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:35.660
The poor actually ate a plentiful diet of
porridge, bread, meats, cheeses, fruits and

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:44.490
plenty of beer to wash it all down.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:50.460
There was also significantly less violence
outside of war than the movies portray.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:55.830
Medieval taverns were relatively civilized,
until of course you go and steal somebody

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:58.600
else’s whore and you get garroted.

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:03.590
So next time you complain about modern-day
life and your long work hours at least you’re

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:09.301
not a slave to some lord or emperor, doing
back-breaking work seven days a week, all

00:05:09.301 --> 00:05:14.630
the while trying to avoid the plague, and
the myriad of other fatal diseases.

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:19.139
And when you walk home at night, the ground
you trod upon is probably nicely paved and

00:05:19.139 --> 00:05:24.800
relatively clean, so just be thankful, because
your street could be covered in the collective

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.690
works of your neighbour’s bowels.

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:41.500
And on that cheery note, thanks for watching.

